  "visualBrief": "Fourteen folded silver roofs and triangular clerestories cover the rail deck. Five island platforms connect to stepped eastern shelters. The clock and lettered glass entrance face Südtiroler Platz, with a lower south concourse at the opposite side.",
  "heightPolicy": "The 206 m deck datum follows the sampled railway corridor. The two street-level landings are fitted separately to the sampled forecourts and transition paving.",
  "nativeAxes": "The two long mapped Südbahn segments set the east-southeast +X rail axis. Südtiroler Platz identifies the west entrance and the mapped island roofs locate the south concourse and east end.",
  "limitations": [
    "PMTiles controls the station footprint, the fourteen folded canopy footprints, eastern shelters and twelve sampled through-track lanes. Roof folds, concourse levels and interior circulation are reconstructed from photographs and standard viewer terrain.",
    "The authored geometry covers the public entrances, station deck and above-ground platforms. Trackside equipment and public concourses are static representations."
  ],
